{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/195784-geist-guiding-or-bringing-shadowguiding-into-geist-without-making-it-wraith","id":195784,"title":"Geist Guiding, or Bringing Shadowguiding into Geist Without Making It Wraith","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Geist: The Sin-Eaters"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-07-12T15:07:59-07:00","id":195784,"title":"Geist Guiding, or Bringing Shadowguiding into Geist Without Making It Wraith","content":"I've been lurking on here for a bit as I prepare to run my first Geist game. I've seen quite a few people suggest expanding and emphasizing the suggestion given in the corebook for having players play one another's geists. And why not? Anyone who ever played Wraith knows what an exhilarating, dramatic, and intense experience this can be.<br /> <br /> But while trying to bring this element into the game, it's too easy to make it a &quot;Sin-Eater versus Geist&quot; relationship. While that would not be a bad game, it is a different game from what's presented in the corebook. So what I've been kicking around in the ol' noggin is a way to introduce &quot;Geist Guiding&quot; into the game without falling into the two situations it seems the developers wanted to avoid:<br /> <br /> (1) That the Geist and the Sin-Eater have an antagonistic relationship<br /> (2) That the Player can lose control of their character as the Geist (and thus another player or the Storyteller) takes control<br /> <br /> Being new to the game, I thought I'd throw out some of these ideas to the community. Folks who have played and ran Geist will definitely have good input and should be able to poke holes in where I might be taking some missteps.<br /> <br /> So here are my crude and rudimentary thoughts so far.<br /> <br /> GEIST GUIDING<br /> As mentioned above, a player would control another player's geist. While playing the geist, the player can speak to the character, appear to them, send them visions, or send them urges. In extreme scenarios they can even activate a Manifestation. But all of this would be predicated upon the Sin-Eater's Synergy rating.<br /> <br /> The higher the Synergy is between a Sin-Eater and her geist, the easier it is for the geist to communicate. As the bond between the two erodes, the geist finds it more difficult to directly communicate and its desires are conveyed in more alien and incomprehensible ways. Geists are not humans, after all. They're also not ghosts. Their &quot;minds,&quot; as they are, do not function like the human brain and often operate on the symbolic level one would expect from an incarnation of death itself. In this capacity, Synergy represents how &quot;in tune&quot; the geist and the Sin-Eater have become with how one another think. For example, at Synergy 10 a geist is able to explicitly whisper to the Sin-Eater any information it wishes to relay, while at Synergy 4 it may only be able to communicate in bizarre and cryptic dreams that are difficult for the Sin-Eater to decipher.<br /> <br /> From a mechanical standpoint, Synergy also affects how a geist uses Urges (more on that below).<br /> <br /> ROLEPLAYING THE GEIST<br /> The geist is not a human or a ghost. While many theories abound as to what exactly a geist is and how it is created, a geist at its core is a symbolic representation of an aspect of death given form. While its thoughts are strange and inhuman, it does think. It has wants and needs. It has a will and, perhaps most frightening of all, it has the ability to plan. Some geists have proven they have the patience to see a decades long plan to its (often horrid) conclusion.<br /> <br /> These aspects of the geist make it a difficult thing to roleplay. The alien and symbolic nature of its thought must be considered but, additionally, the goals and desires of the geist must be established. The geist may even have broad, general goals as well as specific, personal ones. A geist who began its existence as the ghost of a teenage boy killed by police officers may become the Bleeding Boy, a geist of wrath and revenge that seeks to punish authority figures that abuse and overstep their bounds. It may also have a specific goal, however, of killing the officers involved in its own death.<br /> <br /> These goals will vary from geist to geist and, sometimes, will even clash with one another. The Bleeding Boy may be attached to a Sin-Eater who has formed a krewe alongside someone whose geist seeks to maintain order and protect the agents of order - which would, of course, include the police. How the Sin-Eaters deal with this conflict between their geists while trying to maintain Synergy could be the backbone for a series of stories by itself.<br /> <br /> The Player of the Sin-Eater should collaborate directly with the Storyteller to set these goals and personality traits. The Sin-Eater's Archetype and Threshold should be taken into account, but the geist itself should also have three traits to help guide roleplaying: Virtue, Vice, and Purpose.<br /> <br /> Virtue and Vice can differ from the Sin-Eater's Virtue and Vice. Again, these should be chosen with the Archetype, Threshold, and general concept of the geist in mind. The Bleeding Boy above would definitely have Wrath for a Vice, but Temperance wouldn't make much sense for a Virtue. Justice would be a better choice.<br /> <br /> Purpose is the overriding philosophy guiding the geist's actions. While it may (and should) have multiple goals both broad and specific, the Purpose should describe the aspect of death that the geist has become and what it seeks to accomplish in that vein. For the Bleeding Boy, the Purpose would be &quot;Punish authority figures that abuse and overstep their bounds.&quot; For a geist that died after a long and horribly painful battle with cancer, the Purpose may be &quot;Ensure that no one suffers needlessly.&quot; The Purpose can be interpreted in different ways and may not necessarily seem consistent or logical. The geist who seeks to keep others from suffering needlessly may want to protect a child from its abusive parent but may also want to euthanize patients at the local hospital - whether the patients want it or not.<br /> <br /> The Purpose should always be a very broad and never-ending goal. &quot;Catching my killer&quot; would be a specific goal that could be met, completed, and marked off of the to-do list. &quot;Revealing and punishing unknown killers&quot; would be an ongoing Purpose.<br /> <br /> The geist and the Sin-Eater do not necessarily have an antagonistic relationship while its pursuing its Purpose. In fact, the geist would rather convince the Bound that its Purpose is, if not desirable, then at least needed. Worst case scenario, the geist would be fine if the Sin-Eater just threw up his hands, sighed, and said &quot;Whatever. Let's just get it over with.&quot; If the Synergy rating has fallen to 4 or lower, however, the geist may become angry, abusive, or even just whiny in attempting to achieve its Purpose and goals.<br /> <br /> WILLPOWER<br /> In addition to Archetype, Threshold, Virtue, Vice, and Purpose, the Geist also has its own reserve of Willpower. A geist uses its Willpower to fuel Whispers, its ability to communicate with its Sin-Eater, and Urges, its ability to circumvent the Sin-Eater's control and brutally remind them that their relationship is a symbiotic one.<br /> <br /> A geist regains Willpower by fulfilling its Purpose or completing its goals. Every time one of the geist's broad goals is accomplished, it earns back 1 point of Willpower.<br /> <br /> If the geist's Purpose is met, it regains all Willpower that has been spent trying to meet its Purpose. If the geist spent a Willpower point for any other reason (such as giving the Sin-Eater key information about an Avernian Gate that did not relate to it achieving its goal), they do not regain that Willpower point for meeting their Purpose.<br /> <br /> If a very specific goal is completed and marked forever off of the geist's list of goals, at the Storyteller's discretion the gesit *may* gain an additional Permanent dot of Willpower.<br /> <br /> WHISPERS<br /> Whispers are the geist's ability to communicate with the Sin-Eater. For all uses of Whispers, the geist uses a dice pool equal to the Sin-Eater's Synergy rating.<br /> <br /> Dramatic Failure - The geist's attempt at communication goes horribly wrong. The exact opposite of what the geist was attempting to communicate is what the Sin-Eater understands.<br /> Failure - The communication is horribly vague and often frightening, giving the Sin-Eater nothing to work off of and possibly costing them sleep or increasing their stress.<br /> Success - The geist is able to communicate their ideas to the Sin-Eater, but the communication is strictly symbolic and must be interpreted by the Sin-Eater. At the Storyteller's discretion, the Sin-Eater's player may have to make an appropriate roll to puzzle out the meaning.<br /> Exceptional Success - The message is relayed cleanly and clearly with no way that its meaning can be mistaken.<br /> <br /> Other Whispers are rumored to exist, but the following are the most common.<br /> <br /> LEVEL ONE<br /> Dreamspeak - The geist is able to send symbols to the Sin-Eater while they are dreaming.<br /> <br /> LEVEL TWO<br /> A Phantom Word - The geist is able to throw one word into the Sin-Eater's mind. This word might be heard or might present itself as text. It might also appear as a visual representation of the word (Mustang, for instance, could appear as a red sports car or as a stampeding horse).<br /> <br /> LEVEL THREE<br /> Visions - The geist is able to create visions for a Sin-Eater that is awake. No one else can see these visions unless they are somehow psychically observing what the Sin-Eater sees. Costs 1 point of Willpower.<br /> <br /> LEVEL FOUR<br /> Whispers - The geist can whisper a phrase or sentence to the Sin-Eater. Costs 1 point of Willpower.<br /> <br /> LEVEL FIVE<br /> Medium - At this level, the geist can open a bridge of back and forth communication with the Sin-Eater. This communication costs 2 Willpower points and can last for up to one minute. For each additional point of Willpower spent when that minute is up, the bridge will remain open for an additional minute. This additional Willpower can be spent by either the geist or the Sin-Eater, but only the geist can initiate the power by spending 2 Willpower and rolling Synergy.<br /> <br /> <br /> URGES<br /> Where Whispers are communications that occur directly between the geist and its Sin-Eaters, Urges are a geist's way of circumventing the Sin-Eater's consciousness or, at higher levels, bombarding it. Urges can be surgical scalpels used to secretly slice or hammers to bludgeon and shatter. Either way, the use of an Urge threatens the Synergy between the geist and the Bound. The Storyteller should keep track of every time an Urge is used and, when five Urges have been used, a point of Synergy is lost.<br /> <br /> The only way to avoid this Synergy loss is to meet a goal or Purpose of the geist. If a goal or Purpose of the geist is met before five uses of an Urge, then the &quot;Urge counter&quot; gets reset to zero.<br /> <br /> Urges are a geist's last resort and as such they have an inverse relationship with the Synergistic bond. For every use of an urge, the dice pool for the geist is 10 minus Synergy. So a geist whose Sin-Eater has a 7 Synergy would only roll three dice to use an Urge, while a geist whose Sin-Eater had a Synergy of 3 would roll seven dice.<br /> <br /> Dramatic Failure - The geist alerts the Sin-Eater to what they are doing and exactly how to keep them from doing it. The geist loses the ability to use its Urges for the rest of the scene.<br /> Failure - The geist is unable to activate its Urge.<br /> Success - The geist is able to activate the urge.<br /> Exceptional Success - The geist is able to activate its Urge so strongly that one Willpower point spent to activate it is immediately regained.<br /> <br /> There are other Urges that are rumored to exist, but the following are the most common.<br /> <br /> LEVEL ONE<br /> Horrid Visions - Unlike the Vision Whisper, this allows the geist to give the Sin-Eater horrid, nightmarish visions. These visions cannot be so focused as to communicate a goal, but can be focused enough to cause a Sin-Eater to see a child as a blood-caked demon or to see her sleeping boyfriend as a corpse with his throat slit. This Urge can also be used to give the Sin-Eater nightmares while sleeping though, again, communicating a specific desire or request cannot be accomplished.<br /> <br /> LEVEL TWO<br /> Stealing the Key - A geist can activate a Manifestation using any Key associated with its Threshold. The Sin-Eater must roll Wits + Occult to sense the geist doing this. If the Sin-Eater Fails, they have no knowledge of what the geist is doing and cannot stop it. If they Succeed, they can spend a point of Willpower to stop it. If they get an Exceptional Success, they can stop it without the need for spending Willpower. If they roll a Dramatic Failure, however, the geist is able to completely hijack any manifestations made with that key for the remainder of the scene. This Urge requires the geist to spend a Willpower point.<br /> <br /> LEVEL THREE<br /> Skeleton Key - The geist can activate any of the Sin-Eater's Manifestations regardless of what key it requires. The Sin-Eater must roll Wits + Occult to sense the geist doing this. If the Sin-Eater Fails, they have no knowledge of what the geist is doing and cannot stop it. If they Succeed, they can spend a point of Willpower to stop it. If they get an Exceptional Success, they can stop it without the need for spending Willpower. If they roll a Dramatic Failure, however, the geist is able to completely hijack any manifestations made with that key for the remainder of the scene. This Urge requires the geist to spend two Willpower points.<br /> <br /> LEVEL FOUR<br /> Devour - With this Urge, the geist can cause harm to the Sin-Eater or his Mementos to replenish their Willpower. If causing injury to the Sin-Eater, the geist must spend a Willpower point and roll successfully. If successful, the Sin-Eater suddenly suffers a lethal point of damage. This may be a spontaneously broken rib, a laceration across their face, the coughing up of blood, or some other kind of injury. The geist regains two Willpower points for every level of lethal damage it inflicts on the Bound.<br /> <br /> Another possibly even more radical use of this Urge is on Mementos. The geist spends two points of Willpower and causes a Sin-Eater's memento to shatter or decay. The energy released restores the geist to full Willpower.<br /> <br /> These actions will obviously cause a Sin-Eater to think twice about working against the desires of his geist. Unfortunately, a Sin-Eater cannot keep a geist from using Devour on their own bodies. They can, however, prevent the geist from using it on a Memento. The Sin-Eater must roll Wits + Occult to sense the geist attempting to destroy a memento. If the Sin-Eater Fails or rolls a Dramatic Failure, they have no knowledge of what the geist is doing and cannot stop it. If they Succeed, they can spend a point of Willpower to stop it. If they get an Exceptional Success, they can stop it without the need for spending Willpower.<br /> <br /> LEVEL FIVE<br /> Uncontrollable Obsession - The geist forces its desire so deeply into the Sin-Eater's brain that they can think of little else. It becomes an obsession, constantly creeping into their mind when trying to do research, keeping them from sleeping at night, and turning them into a madman with one goal. For every day that the Sin-Eater does not pursue the Obsession, all dice pools are reduced by one until the Sin-Eater is only left with a chance die. The Sin-Eater can stop this reduction for 24 hours by spending a point of Willpower, but they cannot reverse any losses that have already occurred. The only way around this loss is to pursue the Obsession that the geist implanted. Any actions taken while *directly* pursuing the Obsession can ignore the dice pool penalties. This power requires the geist to expend all points of Willpower that they currently possess as they psychically wedge their desire deep into the Bound's mind. A minimum of three Willpower must be spent, so a geist who is down to two Willpower points or less cannot use this power.<br /> <br /> <br /> GEIST CREATION<br /> <br /> A geist has fifteen points with which to build its sheet. The point costs are:<br /> <br /> Willpower - One point per dot<br /> Whispers and Urges - One point per level. Levels must be bought consecutively, i.e. Level Three cannot be purchased without having Levels One and Two.<br /> <br /> I have no ideas yet on how a geist earns experience or otherwise progresses in its abilities.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my novel DARLING that Fangoria said &quot;...is a sweetheart indeed, giving us a fine first glimpse of a formidable talent in the making.&quot; Or try some of my short fiction in anthologies that also include George RR Martin, Neil Gaiman, Chuck Palahniuk, and Jim Butcher. <a href=\"http://brad-hodson.com/bibliography/\" target=\"_blank\">http://brad-hodson.com/bibliography/</a>","edited":{"userid":3478,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3478-bradhodson","user":"BradHodson","date":". 07-12-2014, 06:10 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3478-bradhodson","name":"BradHodson","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-12T17:39:11-07:00","id":195850,"title":"","content":"We actually discussed having Geist-Guides when we started Balance of Shadows, but players elected to control their own Geists to ensure solidity of concept. I don't think having Geist guides is bad though, and my next game I will offer the possibility again.<br /> <br /> I have two concerns with your systems.<br /> <br /> 1) The Geists ability to communicate is often tied to alien-ness, or lack thereof. My concern is your system makes conversation taxing, and I am not crazy about that. Arguing with the voice in their head is a big part (to me) of Sin-Eaters, and making that communication difficult would be a big minus on play (for me.) I'd do away with Whispers and just have the alienness of the Geist be the determinant. The Geist-Guide may choose to have them communicate in fallen leaves, or a speak-n-spell, or whatever, as part of their schtick...it seems to better fit the game than the above system.<br /> <br /> 2) My only real problem with urges is it can damage the PC's Morality without them doing anything. As the Sin-Eater is directly in system punished for low Synergy, This feels a bit unfair, as it can have Synergy drop regardless of how the player is playing her Bound. That bugs me. As a player, I would strongly dislike it. I don't have an issue with Urges, but I think that element should go.<br /> <br /> I'd have level 4 Urge cause some sort of accident, over spontaneous damage, possibly tied to the Geists threshold though that may be too limiting or cause odd things to happen (huh, hit by a divebombing pigeon again?) If the threshold thing does not work I would still have an apparent cause, and the Geist may not be able to do it if there is nothing it can sort of make happen.<br /> <br /> I'd consider something like Urges to help the Geist tip the odds in the Sin-Eaters favor sometimes. Maybe have Synergy as a die pool for that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\">Forum Rules</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">This is my mod voice.</span> This is my goth voice.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/15731-geist-balance-of-shadows-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">[Geist: Balance of Shadows</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/17537-v20-the-conspiracy-of-hrad-%C4%8Dern%C3%A1-hora-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Vampire: The Conspiracy of Hrad \u010cern\u00e1 Hora</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/13838-scion-bohemian-front-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Scion: Bohemian Front</a>][<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/99033-changeling-malibu-dream-house-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling: Malibu Dream House</a>] [<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/268069-demon-night-train-detective-agency-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: Night Train Detective Agency</a>] <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/la94fvk\" target=\"_blank\">[WoD: The Golden Eagle</a>]","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","name":"Baroness Nerak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar56_2.jpeg","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2524"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-12T21:51:19-07:00","id":196021,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Baron Samedi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/195784-geist-guiding-or-bringing-shadowguiding-into-geist-without-making-it-wraith?p=195850#post195850\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> 1) The Geists ability to communicate is often tied to alien-ness, or lack thereof. My concern is your system makes conversation taxing, and I am not crazy about that. Arguing with the voice in their head is a big part (to me) of Sin-Eaters, and making that communication difficult would be a big minus on play (for me.) I'd do away with Whispers and just have the alienness of the Geist be the determinant. The Geist-Guide may choose to have them communicate in fallen leaves, or a speak-n-spell, or whatever, as part of their schtick...it seems to better fit the game than the above system.</div> </div> </div> </div>Good point. Maybe the way to go would be to do away with Whispers but still roll Synergy to see how clearly the message came across?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Baron Samedi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/195784-geist-guiding-or-bringing-shadowguiding-into-geist-without-making-it-wraith?p=195850#post195850\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">2) My only real problem with urges is it can damage the PC's Morality without them doing anything. As the Sin-Eater is directly in system punished for low Synergy, This feels a bit unfair, as it can have Synergy drop regardless of how the player is playing her Bound. That bugs me. As a player, I would strongly dislike it. I don't have an issue with Urges, but I think that element should go.</div> </div> </div> </div>True. I was thinking of Synergy as a two way street here. My reasoning was that if the geist had to resort to using its Urges five times without the Sin-Eater seeking to resolve whatever the geist was trying so desperately to accomplish that this would be representative of a weakening Synergy. Maybe it's best not to have a hard and fast mechanic for Synergy loss in this fashion, instead letting the Storyteller determine how dismissive the Sin-Eater is being of its geist. Plus, the more I think about this, the more I could see the geist's player abusing this and lowering the Sin-Eater's Synergy without good reason.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Baron Samedi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/195784-geist-guiding-or-bringing-shadowguiding-into-geist-without-making-it-wraith?p=195850#post195850\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'd have level 4 Urge cause some sort of accident, over spontaneous damage, possibly tied to the Geists threshold though that may be too limiting or cause odd things to happen (huh, hit by a divebombing pigeon again?) If the threshold thing does not work I would still have an apparent cause, and the Geist may not be able to do it if there is nothing it can sort of make happen.</div> </div> </div> </div>I like that. Something that the Sin-Eater could possibly dismiss as having nothing to do with its geist... until it happens a third or fourth time.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Baron Samedi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/195784-geist-guiding-or-bringing-shadowguiding-into-geist-without-making-it-wraith?p=195850#post195850\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'd consider something like Urges to help the Geist tip the odds in the Sin-Eaters favor sometimes. Maybe have Synergy as a die pool for that.</div> </div> </div> </div>If Whispers is being done away with and the idea behind Urges changes from a psychic smack upside the head to how the geist can affect the world by using the Sin-Eater as a conduit, then the Urges could definitely run the gamut from hurting, annoying, or inconveniencing the Sin-Eater to helping them get out of a bad situation. Powers could be things like the geist spending Willpower to grant the Sin-Eater extra dice on a role, warning them of the gun toting miscreant that's around the corner, or causing the security guard who just witnessed the Sin-Eater's break-in on his security monitor to slip into a deep sleep. There's a lot of possibilities there and, in the interest of helping to cement the give-and-take relationship between the geist and the Sin-Eater, it could definitely become a &quot;carrot and stick&quot; type system to urge (or Urge) the Sin-Eater to follow up on the geist's desires.<br /> <br /> Thanks for the feedback, Baron! Those are exactly the kinds of criticisms I was hoping for. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my novel DARLING that Fangoria said &quot;...is a sweetheart indeed, giving us a fine first glimpse of a formidable talent in the making.&quot; Or try some of my short fiction in anthologies that also include George RR Martin, Neil Gaiman, Chuck Palahniuk, and Jim Butcher. <a href=\"http://brad-hodson.com/bibliography/\" target=\"_blank\">http://brad-hodson.com/bibliography/</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3478-bradhodson","name":"BradHodson","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-13T01:07:28-07:00","id":196107,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BradHodson</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/195784-geist-guiding-or-bringing-shadowguiding-into-geist-without-making-it-wraith?p=196021#post196021\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Good point. Maybe the way to go would be to do away with Whispers but still roll Synergy to see how clearly the message came across?</div> </div> </div> </div>If you want to attach a roll to that, that sounds like a good plan.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> True. I was thinking of Synergy as a two way street here. My reasoning was that if the geist had to resort to using its Urges five times without the Sin-Eater seeking to resolve whatever the geist was trying so desperately to accomplish that this would be representative of a weakening Synergy. Maybe it's best not to have a hard and fast mechanic for Synergy loss in this fashion, instead letting the Storyteller determine how dismissive the Sin-Eater is being of its geist. Plus, the more I think about this, the more I could see the geist's player abusing this and lowering the Sin-Eater's Synergy without good reason. </div> </div> </div>Right. Of course part of this depends on how universal you are going for. A Geistguide among my group won't abuse it to be dickish, so if it was just for us, it would not be a concern. If there are similar circumstances for your group and you are similarly unconcerned, it may be fine. If you want a more general/universal set of guidelines, though, I'd err on not having the Geist be able to rob the PC of Synergy without action on the PC's part.<br /> <br /> I do agree it could be representative of weakening Synergy, but it seems better as a Synergy sin than something the Geist initiates.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I like that. Something that the Sin-Eater could possibly dismiss as having nothing to do with its geist... until it happens a third or fourth time. </div> </div> </div>More in the Haunting motief.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> If Whispers is being done away with and the idea behind Urges changes from a psychic smack upside the head to how the geist can affect the world by using the Sin-Eater as a conduit, then the Urges could definitely run the gamut from hurting, annoying, or inconveniencing the Sin-Eater to helping them get out of a bad situation. Powers could be things like the geist spending Willpower to grant the Sin-Eater extra dice on a role, warning them of the gun toting miscreant that's around the corner, or causing the security guard who just witnessed the Sin-Eater's break-in on his security monitor to slip into a deep sleep. There's a lot of possibilities there and, in the interest of helping to cement the give-and-take relationship between the geist and the Sin-Eater, it could definitely become a &quot;carrot and stick&quot; type system to urge (or Urge) the Sin-Eater to follow up on the geist's desires.<br /> <br /> Thanks for the feedback, Baron! Those are exactly the kinds of criticisms I was hoping for. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> </div> </div> </div>True. Something where helping the Geist could empower it somewhat to do these things could help too...maybe causing car wrecks (or whatever) can give it Willpower it can use to help the player. Or ignoring it gets the Willpower as it can.<br /> <br /> Regardless, happy to help.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\">Forum Rules</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">This is my mod voice.</span> This is my goth voice.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/15731-geist-balance-of-shadows-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">[Geist: Balance of Shadows</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/17537-v20-the-conspiracy-of-hrad-%C4%8Dern%C3%A1-hora-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Vampire: The Conspiracy of Hrad \u010cern\u00e1 Hora</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/13838-scion-bohemian-front-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Scion: Bohemian Front</a>][<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/99033-changeling-malibu-dream-house-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling: Malibu Dream House</a>] [<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/268069-demon-night-train-detective-agency-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: Night Train Detective Agency</a>] <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/la94fvk\" target=\"_blank\">[WoD: The Golden Eagle</a>]","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","name":"Baroness Nerak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar56_2.jpeg","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2524"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}